Notebook[{
Cell["Benchmark: KPZ at LO (functions of p^2)", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"8e68cb27-ec32-4c53-980a-62b9caedeb5a"],

Cell["\<\
Reference: the KPZ LO flow of BMWflow, written in notes/LO_flow_equations.tex \
and notes/kpz_notation.tex (Kloss, Canet, Wschebor, PRE 86, 051124 (2012), \
with f_lambda = 1 and the functions at zero frequency) and coded by hand in \
flow/models/model_kpz.py. This notebook derives the same flow with \
FRGscalarMSR from the ansatz alone and compares it with the notes, exactly, \
at every external momentum p, loop momentum q, angle and dimension d.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"571f2899-ca43-4dce-a876-362a740a7a90"],

Cell["\<\
Why this benchmark: it is the first test of the LO pipeline \
(design/LOPIPELINE.md): couplings that are functions of p^2, a loop at \
generic external momentum whose frequency integral has two pole families (at \
q and at Q = p + q), the anomalous dimensions from f(0) = 1 as the p -> 0 \
limit of the same loop, and the dimensionless flow at fixed p/k.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3490fd0e-64b9-425d-92c3-52ed2f8df588"],

Cell["\<\
Get[\"~/Physics/Sources/FRGscalarMSR/FRGscalarMSR.wl\"];
kpzloDir = \
ExpandFileName[\"~/Physics/Sources/FRGscalarMSR/benchmarks/KPZLO\"];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"86204148-bdc1-41a8-8be0-361445ad94ee"],

Cell["1. Model and ansatz", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"c05a513b-b7e9-44eb-9234-3491dfff23db"],

Cell["\<\
Gamma_k = Int hbar { dt h - nu fnu(-Laplacian) lap h - lam/2 (grad h)^2 } - D \
hbar fD(-Laplacian) hbar, so Gamma(1,1) = i w + nu p^2 fnu(p^2) and \
Gamma(0,2) = -2 D fD(p^2). fn[f, X] is f(-Laplacian) acting on X; \"Functions\
\" ties each function to its reference coupling and states f(0) = 1. The fn \
in the density selects the LO pipeline.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"471a0ac2-8959-48fc-9803-667acc4d60b4"],

Cell["\<\
kpzloTheory = DefineTheory[\"Scalars\" -> {h}, \"Dimension\" -> Dim];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"864c0725-c83b-4789-b383-1bbd328aff33"],

Cell["\<\
kpzloAnsatz = DefineAnsatz[kpzloTheory,
  \"Density\" -> hbar (dt[h] - nuk fn[fnu, lap[h]] - lamk/2 grad[h].grad[h]) \
- Dk hbar fn[fD, hbar],
  \"Couplings\" -> {nuk, lamk, Dk}, \"Functions\" -> {fD -> Dk, fnu -> nuk}];\
\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"9c417cfc-c244-4fbe-a1ce-ea54f1ec1340"],

Cell["2. Symmetries, vertices, regulator, propagator, loops", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"ff178d52-6a14-450d-a699-12336963cf8b"],

Cell["\<\
In LO the symmetries are declarations: the Galilean Ward identity (the 1 of i \
w) is checked at p = 0, the shift symmetry by the vanishing of the p^0 order \
of Gamma(1,1) (so the fnu row can be divided by p^2). The regulators are \
those of kpz_notation.tex with two independent shapes, R_nu = nu q^2 rn and \
R_D = D rd; the notes use one shape r, substituted in the comparison.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ed2ba42a-61f4-45bd-ae14-b6e4a94e7400"],

Cell["\<\
kpzloSymmetries = DeclareSymmetries[kpzloAnsatz,
  Protected[{hbar, h}, \"Frequency\" -> 1, \"Momentum\" -> 0, \"Reason\" -> \
\"Galilean Ward identity (the 1 in front of dt h)\"],
  Protected[{h, hbar}, \"Frequency\" -> 0, \"Momentum\" -> 0, \"Reason\" -> \
\"h -> h + c (shift symmetry)\"],
  NonRenormalised[lamk, \"Reason\" -> \"Galilean invariance\"]];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"932733df-a7ac-41d1-9d1a-bb72b552baa5"],

Cell["kpzloVertices = BuildVertices[kpzloAnsatz];", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"0adcef50-b062-488c-961b-4d0ab8a380d7"],

Cell["\<\
kpzloRegulator = DefineRegulator[kpzloAnsatz, {hbar, h} -> nuk q^2 \
rn[q^2/k^2], {hbar, hbar} -> -2 Dk rd[q^2/k^2], \"Shapes\" -> {rn, rd}];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"f1b356ad-cd59-416b-9b82-9555d0d877ba"],

Cell["\<\
kpzloPropagator = BuildPropagator[kpzloVertices, kpzloRegulator];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"d1e8968f-67ba-4945-919e-72a86570b6ee"],

Cell["\<\
kpzloLoops = BuildLoopIntegrands[kpzloVertices, kpzloPropagator, \
kpzloRegulator];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"d34b85e5-b365-4020-b9ba-766288bff481"],

Cell["3. LO equations, oracle, dimensionless form", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"8fe46480-1c28-4f2b-9dc7-33ce247b7c79"],

Cell["\<\
BuildLOEquations integrates the loop over the frequency by residues at the \
poles of Delta(w, q^2) and Delta(w, Q^2), divides each Gamma2 entry by its \
prefactor (nuk p^2 for fnu, -2 Dk for fD) and takes the p -> 0 limit for eta. \
RunOracle compares the residue result with a numerical frequency integral at \
a random point. AdimensionalEquations writes F(p^2) = f(p^2/k^2) and the flow \
at fixed p/k, which gives the linear part eta f + 2 p^2 f'(p^2).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"55e19b63-02c2-4341-8a7f-5bcb39f24a99"],

Cell["\<\
kpzloEquations = BuildLOEquations[kpzloLoops, kpzloSymmetries];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"c740fa6e-acdb-46f5-b1b4-e969f93dfcc3"],

Cell["RunOracle[kpzloEquations, \"ZeroFlows\" -> True];", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"f6289693-18ff-4c1e-8157-807b7f3ee73e"],

Cell["\<\
kpzloDims = DeriveDimensions[kpzloAnsatz, \"References\" -> {nuk -> \"nu\", \
Dk -> \"D\"}];
kpzloAdim = AdimensionalEquations[kpzloEquations, kpzloDims];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"6b68c6c8-f80a-4251-9e66-2b6aff65688d"],

Cell["\<\
{kpzloAdim[\"Functions\"], kpzloAdim[\"Etas\"], kpzloAdim[\"Linear\"], \
kpzloAdim[\"BetaL\"], kpzloAdim[\"P2Divided\"]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"98fd832d-6c32-471d-a8a3-5c68a446b5d9"],

Cell["4. The reference (LO_flow_equations.tex, kpz_notation.tex)", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"7f557ba7-42af-4972-9c39-9b21920616e0"],

Cell["\<\
Reference.wl transcribes the kernels A_a, A_c, A_d, the loop integrands of \
I_D and I_nu (with I_nu's 1/p^2), the eta matrix and vector, and d_s g = g (d \
- 2 - eta_D + 3 eta_nu), in the notes' variables ph, qh, ch = cos(theta), l_q \
= q^2 (fnu + r), k_q = fD + r, g = lam^2 D/nu^3 k^(d-2).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6cc7c45f-c5de-4f1d-88fd-cc42eeeaf9e7"],

Cell["\<\
Get[FileNameJoin[{kpzloDir, \"Reference.wl\"}]];
Column[{\"D\" -> Short[kpzloRefLoop[\"D\"], 4], \"nu\" -> Short[kpzloRefLoop[\
\"nu\"], 4]}, Spacings -> 2]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"70e68c43-21f4-445c-b4b4-d571a0498332"],

Cell["5. Comparison", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"ce1b21f5-c12f-4a8f-bf49-26f4285b4448"],

Cell["\<\
Checks.wl writes the library's stage in the notes' variables (ap -> ph, aq -> \
qh, CosTheta -> ch, rn = rd = r, alamk^2 = g) and compares with ExactlyZeroQ: \
random rationals for every symbol and every function atom f(x), f'(x), r(x), \
r'(x), so the test is pointwise, not after integration, and holds at symbolic \
d.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"76c0b439-89b9-40b2-a549-73f3bfa44295"],

Cell["\<\
Get[FileNameJoin[{kpzloDir, \"Checks.wl\"}]];
{ExactlyZeroQ[kpzloLibrary[\"Loop\"][[1]] - kpzloRefLoop[\"D\"]], \
ExactlyZeroQ[kpzloLibrary[\"Loop\"][[2]] - kpzloRefLoop[\"nu\"]]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"46a0c133-6e13-46d2-9e7e-392d19af88df"],

Cell["\<\
{ExactlyZeroQ[kpzloLibrary[\"EtaMatrix\"] - kpzloRefEta[\"Matrix\"]], \
ExactlyZeroQ[kpzloLibrary[\"EtaVector\"] - kpzloRefEta[\"Vector\"]]}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"27e2f38b-5fe0-4ad4-9e79-c5a8e26d6e81"],

Cell["6. Summary and the Python export", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"19f0167a-09d4-44da-915f-780129267efc"],

Cell["\<\
The same checks as benchmarks/KPZLO/run.wl and the suite hook \
tests/acceptance/KPZLO.wl. The next cell rebuilds the stage from Pipeline.wl \
(cards hidden) and checks that it gives the same loops, so that this notebook \
and the scripted benchmark cannot drift apart. The last cell writes the \
BMWflow module (docs/handoff/BMWflow_LO.md) to a temporary directory.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5636e23c-b273-41cb-a1ea-7ad308aaecbb"],

Cell["\<\
kpzloResults = kpzloChecks[];
kpzloSummary[kpzloResults]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"cc6401e8-6ee6-4a85-a4e8-53f9d6aa5b8d"],

Cell["\<\
If[AllTrue[kpzloResults, #Pass &], \"all checks pass\", Abort[]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"402fb3d5-b623-4460-b7e1-620b1e899314"],

Cell["\<\
nbLoops = kpzloAdim[\"Loop\"];
Block[{kpzloAdim, Print}, Get[FileNameJoin[{kpzloDir, \"Pipeline.wl\"}]]; \
If[kpzloAdim[\"Loop\"] === nbLoops, \"same stage as Pipeline.wl\", Abort[]]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"c5320ebf-2c00-4f0b-a8cc-ab872c2dc6a5"],

Cell["\<\
ExportPython[kpzloAdim, \"G\" -> alamk^2, \"Model\" -> \"KPZ\", \"File\" -> \
FileNameJoin[{$TemporaryDirectory, \"KPZ_LO.py\"}]]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"1c2b95f8-ab7a-421d-b86b-1adc009d5990"]
},
FrontEndVersion->"14.3 for Linux x86 (64-bit) (July 8, 2025)",
StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb",
ExpressionUUID->"2a12a001-242d-48f8-ac96-1aa350b0fea8"
]
